@startuml post_deletion_flow
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "Inter, Segoe UI, sans-serif"
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam roundCorner 8
skinparam shadowout false

skinparam wrapWidth 220
skinparam maxMessageSize 150

skinparam activity {
    BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
    BorderColor #64748B
    FontColor #0F172A
    FontSize 11
    ArrowColor #475569
    ArrowFontSize 10
}

skinparam activityDiamond {
    BackgroundColor #FEF3C7
    BorderColor #D97706
    FontColor #92400E
}

title **Modern Laravel Blog - Author Dashboard: Post Deletion & Confirmation Modal Flow**

|#EFF6FF|Author (Browser & Alpine.js)|
|#FEFCE8|Alpine.js Confirmation Modal|
|#F0FDF4|PostPolicy & Controller|
|#FAF5FF|Storage (Public Disk) & SQLite DB|

|Author (Browser & Alpine.js)|
start
:Author views posts list on **/dashboard/posts**;
:Author clicks "Delete" button next to a post row;

|Alpine.js Confirmation Modal|
:Alpine.js intercepts event via **@click="openDeleteModal(post)"**;
:Prevent default immediate form submission;
:Set modal state:
- **confirmDeleteModal = true**
- **postToDelete = { id: post.id, title: post.title }**;
:Render modal dialog with **x-transition** overlay:
- Warning icon & title
- "Are you sure you want to delete '[Title]'?"
- Explanation that this action cannot be undone;

|Author (Browser & Alpine.js)|
if (User Decision?) then (Cancel / Press ESC / Click Backdrop)
    |Alpine.js Confirmation Modal|
    :Alpine.js catches **@keydown.escape.window** or Cancel button;
    :Reset **confirmDeleteModal = false**;
    :Modal fades out with smooth transition;
    |Author (Browser & Alpine.js)|
    :Action aborted; no data altered; <<#F1F5F9>>
    stop
else (Confirm Delete)
    |Alpine.js Confirmation Modal|
    :Author clicks danger "Yes, Delete Article" button;
    :Submit dynamic delete form via **DELETE /dashboard/posts/{post}**;

    |PostPolicy & Controller|
    :Request intercepted by **DashboardPostController@destroy(Post $post)**;
    :Execute **Gate::authorize('delete', $post)**;
    :Evaluate **PostPolicy@delete(User $user, Post $post)**:
    ""return $user->id === $post->author_id"";

    if (Is Authenticated User the Post Author?) then (no - Unauthorized)
        |PostPolicy & Controller|
        :Abort with **403 Forbidden**\n("This action is unauthorized."); <<#FEE2E2>>
        stop
    else (yes - Authorized)
        |Storage (Public Disk) & SQLite DB|
        if (Post has associated image file?) then (yes)
            if (File exists in storage/app/public/posts?) then (yes)
                :Remove file from disk:\n""Storage::disk('public')->delete($post->image)"";
            else (no)
                :File does not exist on disk;
            endif
        else (no)
            :No image attached;
        endif

        :Execute record deletion:\n""$post->delete()"";
        :Delete row from **posts** table in SQLite database;

        |PostPolicy & Controller|
        :Flash success message to session:\n""with('success', 'Article deleted successfully!')"";
        :Redirect back to **route('dashboard.posts.index')**;

        |Author (Browser & Alpine.js)|
        :Dashboard re-renders with the post removed from the table;
        :Alpine.js renders auto-dismissing confirmation alert\n("Article deleted successfully!"); <<#DCFCE7>>
        stop
    endif
endif

@enduml
